# Mintlify CLI ignore file (gitignore-style globs; see @mintlify/common's
# mintIgnore.js / the `ignore` npm package for exact matching semantics).
# Read by `mint validate`, `mint broken-links`, etc. via the shared
# prebuild file-categorization pass.
#
# app_docs/ holds ADW-generated feature-doc artifacts (worker-authored,
# per-issue build notes) — not customer-facing docs, not wired into
# docs.json navigation, and already treated as structurally-internal by
# this repo's own custom checks (see check-nav-coverage.mjs, check-anchors.mjs,
# check-heading-hierarchy.mjs). Excluding it here keeps Mintlify's own file
# walk consistent with that existing convention, and stops a new artifact's
# heading punctuation (e.g. a bare "%") from tripping mint's URI-decode step
# in `mint broken-links` (MNE-2313).
app_docs/
